{"kind":"request","text":"Decide E4 failure history against C4's old signer/store stop rule before source application. Concrete external API /private/tmp/artroom-e4-proposed-source-20261115/API.md and independent review /private/tmp/artroom-e4-c4-fence-review-20261115/README.md expose this one contract conflict.\n\nRuling347916 requires authorization persistence before its custody signing write. Proposal: retain a pre-sign permission under the same fence before invoking the signer; permission references gesture position and exact materialized act. If signer fails or later custody write fails after a signature may exist, keep that true authorization/permission history. Do not claim a held signing, dispatch unheld bytes, roll back evidence or permit another envelope for that position. A retry of that same position stops authorization-used; a new explicit member gesture may append another position. This preserves the first-build no-second-envelope rule even after uncertainty.\n\nD12 scope-client note398–407 says signer/store stops change no store. That promise cannot remain literal while the earlier E4 permission persists. Please decide: may those stops retain this permission, with the draft still editable and its next explicit submit a new gesture, while pre-permission shape/state/busy/owner/descriptor/admission stops stay write-free? Proposed local reason is authorization-used. Descriptor stop remains proposed descriptor-mismatch. No E4 implementation is applied and no runtime ran. E4 remains port+memory; client dispatch/cancellation/deadline enforcement will receive separate source review, using the existing coordinating fence without network await or added timer.","body":{"conditions":"Decide persistent pre-sign permission after signer or custody-write failure, same-position retry stop authorization-used, and C4's resulting explicit-new-gesture behavior. Do not fabricate rollback or past authority.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b1